    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d460">

                <pb facs="0512" n="462" sameAs="frus:frus1894/pg462"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Guzmán to Mr. Gresham.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the Republic of Nicaragua</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1894-05-10"><hi rendition="#italic">May 10,
                                1894</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Pursuant to the conversation I had with
                    your excellency on the 7th instant, I have sent to the President of Nicaragua a
                    cablegram in which I state that the Government of the United States would be
                    pleased to see that the utmost harmony may prevail between Nicaragua and the
                    canal company, and that it would be much gratified if all proceedings against
                    the said company were revoked.</p>
                <p>I reiterate, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">H. Guzmán.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
